        why_en: "A p.1036 itemises it: two high-energy phosphates per aminoacyl-tRNA, an additional ATP whenever proofreading hydrolyses a wrongly activated amino acid, one GTP in the first elongation step and another in translocation. Hence “the energy derived from the hydrolysis of more than four NTPs to NDPs is required for the formation of each peptide bond of a polypeptide”. SUMMARY 27.2 restates it as at least four high-energy phosphate equivalents that “are required to generate each peptide bond, an energy investment required to guarantee fidelity of translation” (A p.1041). The comparison is what makes the number bite: 122 kJ/mol spent against a peptide bond whose own hydrolysis releases only about 21 kJ/mol.",
        why_cn: "A 印刷页 1036 是一项一项列出来的：**每个氨酰-tRNA 两个高能磷酸**；**校对每水解掉一个被错误活化的氨基酸就再加一个 ATP**；**延长第一步一个 GTP**，**移位再一个**。因此**每形成多肽中的一个肽键，需要由四个以上的 NTP 水解成 NDP 所提供的能量**。SUMMARY 27.2 又重申为：**至少四个高能磷酸当量「是产生每一个肽键所必需的，这笔能量投资是为了保证翻译的保真度」**（A 印刷页 1041）。真正让这个数字有分量的是那个比较：**花掉 122 kJ/mol，去造一个自身水解只放出约 21 kJ/mol 的肽键。**"
