        why_en: "A pp.1020-1021 and MECHANISM FIGURE 27-19. Both classes form the enzyme-bound aminoacyl adenylate in step one; the second step differs. A class I enzyme transfers the aminoacyl group to the 2-position hydroxyl of the terminal adenosine and then moves it to the 3-position by transesterification, while a class II enzyme delivers it directly to the 3-position hydroxyl. The classes also bind opposite faces of their tRNA substrates, and TABLE 27-7 splits the twenty enzymes ten and ten. Lehninger adds that there is no evidence the two classes share a common ancestor, and that the reasons for having two classes for essentially identical processes remain obscure.",
        why_cn: "A 印刷页 1020-1021 及 MECHANISM FIGURE 27-19。**两类在第一步都形成结合在酶上的氨酰腺苷酸**；差别在**第二步**。**I 类**把氨酰基转到末端腺苷的 **2 位羟基**，再通过**转酯**挪到 3 位；**II 类**则**直接**送到 3 位羟基。两类还**结合在 tRNA 相对的两个面上**，而 TABLE 27-7 把二十个酶**十个对十个**地分开。Lehninger 还补充说：**没有证据表明两类同源**，而**为什么本质相同的过程要用两类酶来做，至今不清楚**。"
